        <mxCell id="c52" value="&lt;i&gt;Outlined in teal: the two input cells, B5 (the row input, across) and B6 (the column input, down), which sit on this sheet because a Data Table&#x27;s input cells must. In blue: the corner cell A41, the sum of column V over the families to buy (FUR-BNH, FUR-NGT, FUR-TBL). In coral: C44, all the crew time removed at the quote as it is, which equals the annual effect of buying them with the crew reduced, 255,481; the row of none removed, C42, is the 334,636 they cost with the crew kept, shown with a minus sign. Every grid cell is the one array formula {=TABLE(B5,B6)}, shown in the bar.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="350" width="860" height="68" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
